   679	# PLAN-166 W1-B — structural asserts for the release.yml verdict delta +
   680	# ancestry gate (F2 server side; re-pass r15+r17+r18, debate r3 scoped
   680	# ancestry gate (F2 server side; re-pass r15+r17+r18, debate r3 scoped
   681	# VETO). Merged verbatim from the W1-B slice file
   682	# (test_release_workflow_asserts_w1b.py) by the PLAN-166 ceremony
   683	# assembler — one runnable asserts file per the W1 pack discipline. Only
   684	# names that would collide with the W1-A section above were renamed
   685	# (_MARKER → _MARKER_W1B, _LIVE_WF/_STAGED_WF → _W1B_*).
   686	#
   687	# What is pinned here, and why each pin exists:
   688	# - The gate step exists, carries NO continue-on-error, and FAILS CLOSED
   689	#   on CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1 — the step-15 neighbourhood has
   690	#   two escape hatches keyed to that var (`continue-on-error:` and the
   691	#   empty `--parent-sha ""` bind, which the validator only binds when
   692	#   non-empty); the new gate must never inherit the switch.
   693	# - The delta decision is DELEGATED to
   694	#   .claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py (the reference
   695	#   implementation) — never re-implemented in bash.
   696	# - Ancestry covers BOTH the reviewed parent AND GITHUB_SHA (r18:
   697	#   parent-only lets the tag-without-push / orphan-verdict scenario pass).
   698	# - PINNED ORDER: Verify tag GPG signature → Validate pair-rail verdict →
   699	#   delta → ancestry.
   700	# - The job keeps the exact name `release-gate` — the W1-A
   701	#   await-release-gate poller resolves the job BY NAME via the Actions
   702	#   jobs endpoint; renaming the job silently breaks the npm-publish gate.
   703	# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
